cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the PET-KLS Pipeline repository.
  The accompanying scientific manuscript is listed under references.
title: "PET-KLS Pipeline"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Monteiro"
    given-names: "Sara"

abstract: >-
  PET-KLS is a Python pipeline for constructing subject-specific PET
  similarity connectomes from regional voxel-wise standardized uptake
  value ratio distributions. Regional probability density functions are
  estimated using kernel density estimation, compared using symmetric
  Kullback-Leibler divergence, and transformed into bounded similarity
  weights.

repository-code: "https://github.com/PET-KLS/PETKLS_pipeline"
url: "https://github.com/PET-KLS/PETKLS_pipeline"

identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://github.com/PET-KLS/PETKLS_pipeline"
    description: "PET-KLS Pipeline GitHub repository"

license: "CC-BY-4.0"

keywords:
  - PET
  - amyloid PET
  - Kullback-Leibler divergence
  - Kullback-Leibler similarity
  - connectome
  - brain networks
  - neuroimaging
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - kernel density estimation

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Amyloid PET Similarity Networks in Preclinical Alzheimer's Disease
      Reveal Early Dynamic Topological Reorganization
